Arpile 32CDF is the firmware for the Arpile Cyberdeck Project.

Microcontroller Unit: Waveshare ESP32 P4 Nano
Display: ILI9488 3.5" 480x320
Audio codec chip: ES8311 (integrated into the ESP32 P4 Nano board)
Additional Storage: MicroSD card (slot integrated into the ESP32 P4 Nano board)
Input method: Keyboard (using USB-A)

ESP-IDF Based

Display wiring:
CS   → GPIO23
RST  → GPIO4
DC   → GPIO20
MOSI → GPIO5
SCK  → GPIO21
LED  → GPIO22

Rules:
- Treat this document as the source of truth for the hardware configuration.
- Do not change GPIO assignments without explicit approval.
- Do not add hardware components or peripherals without explicit approval.
- Do not modify working hardware drivers unnecessarily.
- Keep hardware-specific code isolated and modular.
- Test hardware components independently before integrating them into the main firmware.
- Do not assume undocumented hardware capabilities; verify them first.
- Prefer ESP-IDF APIs and existing project components over unnecessary custom implementations.
- The Device should be capable of being independent from the SD card.

